  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN each. Determine the number of good pairs.\n\nA pair (i,j)(i,j)(i,j) (1≤i,j≤N)(1\\le i,j \\le N)(1≤i,j≤N) is said to be good if **all** of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n\ni&lt;j;i \\lt j;i&lt;j;\nAi=Bj;A_i = B_j;Ai​=Bj​;\nAj=Bi;A_j = B_i;Aj​=Bi​;\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\n\nDescription of each test case:\n\n\n\nFirst line contains an integer NNN - denoting the length of the arrays.\nSecond line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…ANA_1, A_2, \\dots A_NA1​,A2​,…AN​ - denoting the array AAA.\nThird line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…BNB_1, B_2, \\dots B_NB1​,B2​,…BN​ - denoting the array BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of good pairs.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n1 2 3\n3 2 1\n4\n1 2 3 4\n5 6 6 7\n3\n10 10 10\n10 10 10\n4\n4 8 1 1\n8 4 1 1",
        "output": "1\n0\n3\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: The only good pair (i,j)(i,j)(i,j) is (1,3)(1,3)(1,3). Here,\n\n1<31 \\lt 31<3\nA1=1A_1 = 1A1​=1 and B3=1B_3 = 1B3​=1. Thus, A1=B3A_1 = B_3A1​=B3​.\nA3=3A_3 = 3A3​=3 and B1=3B_1 = 3B1​=3. Thus, A3=B1A_3 = B_1A3​=B1​.\n\nTest Case 222: There are no good pairs.\nTest Case 333: There are 333 good pairs (i,j)(i,j)(i,j). These are (1,2),(1,3),(1,2), (1,3),(1,2),(1,3), and (2,3)(2,3)(2,3).\nTest Case 444: There are 222 good pairs (i,j)(i,j)(i,j). These are (1,2)(1,2)(1,2) and (3,4)(3,4)(3,4)."
      }
    ]
  },
